# The whole game as the original runs it, levels 1 to 5 in one session, for
# checking the port's objects against it frame by frame: a one-player game,
# the ship kept alive (the shield refilled, no death, no wall), the shops
# skipped, fire held so the ship shoots up from x 160; the ship steered and
# the bosses helped as each level's own run does it (level 2's spider: under
# its right eye, its left, the middle, level2-spider.exp; level 4's bosses at
# 1 hit point and the ship under them, level4-kill.exp; level 5's end boss
# circled until its parts are gone (at frame 9000 they are taken as gone),
# then the ship under its core, level5-boss.exp). A level not won by a
# frame of its own (1: 9000, 2: 15000, 3: 20000, 4: 9000, 5: 16000) is taken
# as won ($A07 and $A6C set, logged with $F0F0).
# Logged every frame ($3E42, full-run-frame.ini), every token taken ($4FF8),
# every enemy destroyed ($6250), and every object's update as the update
# walk calls it ($3EC8) on the enemy list ($B4C), the effects' list ($BAE)
# and the scenery objects' list ($C10): $B0B0, the walk's return address
# (which list) and the object's first 52 bytes.
# Run with --trace fdc.
expect prompt read sector sector=0x1 .*tr=0x0 .*addr=0x6760e
stage level-run-shield.ini
stage level-run-nodeath.ini
stage level-run-nowall.ini
stage level-run-noshop.ini
stage full-run-frame.ini
stage full-run-obj.ini
stage full-run-won.ini
stage weapons-take.ini
stage waves-kill.ini
stage level2-right.ini
stage level2-left.ini
stage level2-middle.ini
stage level4-hp1.ini
stage level4-x128.ini
stage level4-x192.ini
stage level4-x160.ini
stage level4-x120.ini
stage level4-x200.ini
stage level4-hold.ini
stage level5-down-left.ini
stage level5-down-right.ini
stage level5-up-left.ini
stage level5-up-right.ini
stage level5-core.ini
stage level5-core-hold.ini
stage level5-bare.ini
stage level5-ending.ini
stage full-run-start.ini
# Hatari 2.6 loses its breakpoints when a hit adds the 16th (it grows the
# array without copying it): grow it here (to 40), outside any hit, then
# clear it.
debug b pc = $1
debug b pc = $2
debug b pc = $3
debug b pc = $4
debug b pc = $5
debug b pc = $6
debug b pc = $7
debug b pc = $8
debug b pc = $9
debug b pc = $a
debug b pc = $b
debug b pc = $c
debug b pc = $d
debug b pc = $e
debug b pc = $f
debug b pc = $10
debug b pc = $11
debug b pc = $12
debug b pc = $13
debug b pc = $14
debug b pc = $15
debug b pc = $16
debug b pc = $17
debug b pc = $18
debug b pc = $19
debug b pc = $1a
debug b pc = $1b
debug b pc = $1c
debug b pc = $1d
debug b pc = $1e
debug b pc = $1f
debug b pc = $20
debug b pc = $21
debug b pc = $22
debug b pc = $23
debug b pc = $24
debug b pc = $25
debug b pc = $26
debug b pc = $27
debug b pc = $28
debug b all
debug b pc = $7a50 :once :trace :file {run}/full-run-start.ini
disk-a {disk2}
sleep 8
fire
sleep 4
fire
expect level1-read read sector sector=0x3 .*tr=0xc .*addr=0x3e
quiet level1-loaded 3
